[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/comments/6555660210","html_url":"https://github.com/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/33#issuecomment-6555660210","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/33","id":6555660210,"node_id":"IC_kwDORt12rc8AAAABhr9vsg","user":{"login":"alexar76","id":86793359,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NzkzMzU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86793359?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-01T09:41:56Z","updated_at":"2026-11-01T09:41:56Z","body":"Some data for point 1 and for what the check could cover, from HISTOR, which reads `tools/list` from the servers in the official MCP registry and records every change (data: https://histor.modelmarket.dev/datasets/, CC BY 4.0).\n\n- **Annotation-only changes happen.** From 23 to 31 October HISTOR recorded 272 changes in which only annotations changed, with name, description, inputSchema and outputSchema identical. `destructiveHint` went false→true on 70 tools and `readOnlyHint` true→false on 66. The direction that relaxes an approval policy occurs too: `readOnlyHint` false→true on 10 tools, `destructiveHint` true→false on 9. A pin over the description, or over the four fields without annotations, misses all of them. A text diff of the description shows nothing either, so the re-approval prompt should name the hint that flipped.\n- **A version number is not a pin.** In HISTOR's records of remote servers from 24 September to 20 October, 81.3% of changes (17,401 of 21,401 with both versions known) kept the same `serverInfo.version`. A client that asks again only when the version changes misses most of them, which could be a finding of its own.\n- **Server instructions.** The `instructions` returned by `initialize` reach the model in clients that use them, and they change too: ScraperWatch's public change log (https://scraperwatch.com/mcp-changes/) recorded instruction changes on 27 endpoints in its first two days. They belong in the pin.\n- **Legitimate changes are frequent.** In the same eight days HISTOR recorded 15,135 changes to the four fields on 7,232 servers. Re-approval will fire often, so the diff has to be short and readable, or users will approve without reading it.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/comments/6555660210/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/comments/6709804604","html_url":"https://github.com/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/33#issuecomment-6709804604","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/33","id":6709804604,"node_id":"IC_kwDORt12rc8AAAABj-9-PA","user":{"login":"emmanuelorta","id":253105980,"node_id":"U_kgDODxYXPA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/253105980?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta","html_url":"https://github.com/emmanuelorta","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-07T16:25:44Z","updated_at":"2026-11-07T16:25:44Z","body":"A concrete shape for the step: at review time, keep a hash per tool **per part** (description, inputSchema, annotations) rather than one hash per server, so a later mismatch says which part moved and a routine description edit can be re-approved quickly while a widened schema or a dropped `readOnlyHint` gets a closer look. Then re-list and compare on every connect.\n\nWhy it matters in practice: across the public MCP Registry, at least 16.4% of servers that list tools changed them between two reads about ten days apart ([live data](https://crawlcheck.io/research/mcp-tool-changes), [public feed of each change](https://crawlcheck.io/mcp/changes)). A published hash definition and test vectors are at [https://crawlcheck.io/spec/mcp-lockfile](https://crawlcheck.io/spec/mcp-lockfile) and [here](https://github.com/emmanuelorta/crawlcheck-core/blob/main/sdk/test/fixtures/continuity.json) if the play wants something to point at.\n\n(Disclosure: I build CrawlCheck. The data, spec and vectors are free; the test file is MIT.)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/comments/6709804604/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/comments/6712051397","html_url":"https://github.com/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/33#issuecomment-6712051397","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/33","id":6712051397,"node_id":"IC_kwDORt12rc8AAAABkBHGxQ","user":{"login":"alexar76","id":86793359,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NzkzMzU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86793359?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-07T19:34:47Z","updated_at":"2026-11-07T19:34:47Z","body":"A follow-up on the hash definition. HISTOR's tool-set digest and CrawlCheck's `jcs_v1.tools_sha256` are the same function: the four contract members (`description` as `\"\"` and `inputSchema` as `{}` when absent, `outputSchema` only when the server sent an object), sorted by name in UTF-16 code units, RFC 8785, SHA-256 as an SRI string. I checked it both ways. Both of CrawlCheck's published vectors give the same digests in HISTOR's code. Six tool sets from HISTOR's records (3 to 28 tools, one with fractional numbers in its schemas, all with non-ASCII text) posted to `/api/v1/mcp/lock` came back with the digest HISTOR had recorded for each.\n\nFor the step, that means the pin can be one value which two independent public records compute the same way, and a reviewer can check a client's pin against either. Annotations are outside that digest in both. CrawlCheck covers them separately in `extras_sha256`; HISTOR records them under a different extras digest that is not RFC 8785, so those two do not match. A check that wants the `readOnlyHint` cases should pin the extras too, as the issue proposes.\n\nHISTOR now also compares the digests in CrawlCheck's public change feed with its own every day and publishes the result, disagreements included:\nhttps://histor.modelmarket.dev/datasets/xcheck-crawlcheck/\n\nThe first run, on 7 November, found 8 events with the digest: 7 agree, 0 disagree, and one server HISTOR had not read within 24 hours.\n\nHISTOR's rule:\nhttps://github.com/alexar76/histor/blob/eb3c6c60aad13900330c634822c1e69292579094/docs/labels.md\n\nOne of the six sets, by its digest:\nhttps://histor.modelmarket.dev/api/v1/toolsets/sha256-0QjeQokTt8cWjkULrBONvt%2F1oWELrTOmdfknXnu%2BiIY%3D\n\n(We run HISTOR.)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/comments/6712051397/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/comments/6712103956","html_url":"https://github.com/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/33#issuecomment-6712103956","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/33","id":6712103956,"node_id":"IC_kwDORt12rc8AAAABkBKUFA","user":{"login":"emmanuelorta","id":253105980,"node_id":"U_kgDODxYXPA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/253105980?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta","html_url":"https://github.com/emmanuelorta","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-07T19:39:41Z","updated_at":"2026-11-07T19:39:41Z","body":"Thanks for checking both ways. Confirmed from our side: the set you linked (`sha256-0QjeQokT…`, 3 tools) returns that digest from POST /api/v1/mcp/lock, and the reelquoteai row in your first report is just timing; a fresh read today still gives `sha256-5vEPfX1K…` (33 tools).\n\nOne update on extras: since our follow-up on modelcontextprotocol/registry#82, CrawlCheck's `extras_sha256` uses HISTOR's extras construction rather than RFC 8785, so the two extras digests now match too. For crawlcheck.io/mcp both are `sha256-G44DGgW7…`. That means a pin covering tools plus annotations (the readOnlyHint cases) can also be checked against either record. If you see an extras mismatch on any server, tell us and we'll treat it as a bug on our side.\n\n(We run CrawlCheck.)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/comments/6712103956/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/comments/6712138890","html_url":"https://github.com/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/33#issuecomment-6712138890","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/33","id":6712138890,"node_id":"IC_kwDORt12rc8AAAABkBMcig","user":{"login":"Dee-Tee11","id":216906516,"node_id":"U_kgDODO27FA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216906516?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dee-Tee11","html_url":"https://github.com/Dee-Tee11","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dee-Tee11/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dee-Tee11/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dee-Tee11/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dee-Tee11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dee-Tee11/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dee-Tee11/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dee-Tee11/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dee-Tee11/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dee-Tee11/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-07T19:42:56Z","updated_at":"2026-11-07T19:42:56Z","body":"Thanks for the info guys i have been reading all the comments and feel exited with all the stuff you guys are bringing up !\nI will open this PR tomorow morning !","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/comments/6712138890/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]